From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:17:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 172/207] runner scan: STATED reads a stacked column at its
 lone `=`
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under inline math and STATED (trace_whole), a line that is only `=` (or `= `)
right after exactly two lines, a literal and an operator line, opens an inline
cell for the whole column:

    264,278,028,996,235,349,740,985,471,434
    +771,565,915,835,769,397,012,014,492,734
    = ?

W7 and S2 R5 replies hand-add these columns (27 missed tasks, about 28% of the
missed hand-work); no form read them, since inline needs the expression on the
`=` line. Operands are plain non-negative integer literals (thousands groups,
no leading zero, at most 120 chars), the operator `+ - * ×` (not `x`). A
longer column or a multiplication table (a literal or operator line above the
first operand) refuses, and a join cue keeps the model's value as for
`1119 + 392 =`. The scanner keeps the last three lines only under STATED.

Replay of W7 + R5 (784 files) through route.Dispatch, bank v7: STATED off
byte-identical (2911 cells); on, 63 cells gained, 0 lost, all equal to
CPython. Goldens, near-miss refusals, a graph-bank proof with a mutated
operand, and four negative controls.

(cherry picked from commit 141531470e35d243951af01b2b99fb7c358e527c)
